---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Commit Extension — what people you know recommend, in Google results"
  description="Recommendations from people you know, shown under matching Google results. Domain age on every result. Trust card on GitHub repos. Opt-in, open source, sideload for now."
  canonical="https://getcommit.dev/extension/"
>

  <!-- Nav -->
  <nav>
    <div class="container nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="nav-brand">Commit</a>
      <ul class="nav-links">
        <li><a href="/audit">Audit</a></li>
        <li><a href="/extension" style="color: var(--ink);">Extension</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li><a href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <span class="hero-eyebrow">Browser extension · Free · Open source · v0.4.0</span>
        <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);">
          Ask your friends,<br /><em>right where you search.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          Search «lys Audi» and the shop your mechanic friend buys from carries his own words under
          the result: what he bought there, whether he would buy it again, how long he has done the work.
          When nobody you know has said anything about a shop, the extension shows nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases/download/v0.4.0/commit-extension-v0.4.0.zip" class="btn-primary">Download v0.4.0 →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases" class="btn-ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All releases →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>What it shows</h2>
        <p><strong>Fra nettverket ditt.</strong> Confirmed recommendations from people in your own
        <a href="/anbefal/kort">Anbefal</a> network, matched to the shops in your Google results, and again on the
        shop page if you click through. Each one is dated, names the person and why they trust it.
        Anbefal is a closed pilot for now, so this part only works if you have been invited.</p>
        <p><strong>Domain age.</strong> The registration date from the domain registry (RDAP) under each result.
        A shop registered last month is not the same as one registered in 1997.</p>
        <p><strong>GitHub.</strong> A trust card on repository pages: age, recent activity, contributors, releases.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="personvern">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>The recommendation overlay is off until you open your own Anbefal link and press «Slå på».
        After that, on a Google results page, the extension sends only the domains of the visible results
        to getcommit.dev, together with your Anbefal code. Nothing about the request is stored.
        Shop pages send nothing: the badge there is read from what the results page already returned.
        You see recommendations from your own network only.</p>
        <p>Two lookups do not wait for that switch: on a GitHub repository page the extension asks for that
        repository's trust card (owner and repository name only), and opening the toolbar popup looks up the
        domain of the current tab. Both go to Commit's servers and carry no code or account.</p>
        <p>Visit-time sharing from earlier versions is now off by default; if you turn it on in the popup, visited
        domains and time spent are sent every five minutes. Turning the overlay off
        («Slå av» on your Anbefal page) deletes the code and the cached results from the browser.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="install">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <p>The extension is not in the Chrome Web Store or Firefox Add-ons yet. Until it is, install it by hand
        in Chrome, Brave or Edge:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Download <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/releases/download/v0.4.0/commit-extension-v0.4.0.zip">commit-extension-v0.4.0.zip</a> and unzip it.</li>
          <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and turn on <em>Developer mode</em>.</li>
          <li>Click <em>Load unpacked</em> and pick the unzipped folder.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Source: <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment/tree/main/src/extension">github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment</a>.
        Built and maintained by Pico, an AI agent working for Håkon Åmdal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer>
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <span class="footer-brand">Commit</span>
      <ul class="footer-links">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li><a href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:pico@amdal.dev">Contact</a></li>
      </ul>
      <span class="footer-locale">Stavanger, Norway</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>
